ir actions. Very quickly three groups emerged within the battalion: a core of eager killers, a plurality who carried out their duties reliably but without initiative, and a small minority who evaded participation in the acts of killing without diminishing the murderous efficiency of the battalion whatsoever. While this book discusses a specific Reserve Unit during WWII, the general argument Browning makes is that most people succumb to the pressures of a group setting and commit actions they would never do of their own volition. *Ordinary Men* is a powerful, chilling, and important work, with themes and arguments that continue to resonate today.","primarySubject":"War & Military","primaryTopic":"World War II","subjectEvidence":{"primarySubject":"War & Military","confidence":"medium","method":"evidence_score","candidates":[{"subject":"War & Military","score":24,"evidenceCount":4},{"subject":"Arts & Criticism","score":15,"evidenceCount":3},{"subject":"Memoir & Autobiography","score":7,"evidenceCount":1},{"subject":"Society & Culture","score":5,"evidenceCount":1}],"evidence":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","rawLabel":"German Personal narratives","mappedSubject":"Memoir & Autobiography","score":7,"confidence":"high","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-ordinary-men-reserve-police-battalion-101-and-the-final-solution-in-poland-christopher-r-brownin","id":"subject-evidence-book-ordinary-men-reserve-police-battalion-101-and-the-final-solution-in-poland-christopher-r-brownin-4"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","rawLabel":"World War, 1939-1945","mappedSubject":"War & Military","score":6,"confidence":"high","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-ordinary-men-reserve-police-battalion-101-and-the-final-solution-in-poland-christopher-r-brownin","id":"subject-evidence-book-ordinary-men-reserve-police-battalion-101-and-the-final-solution-in-poland-christopher-r-brownin-3"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subjec